# Second Brain — Roadmap

Local-first personal AI memory. Reliability over cleverness.

## Done

- Automatic memory extraction from chat (Ollama + offline fallback)
- Entities, relationships, facts, aliases, confidence, sources, timestamps
- Active / superseded / pinned / important state
- Duplicate merge, conflict detection, supersession, memory history
- Knowledge graph (real SQLite data): pan, zoom, focus, expand, filters
- Hybrid search (keyword + semantic + graph) and multi-hop RAG
- KNOWN / UNKNOWN / UNCERTAIN answers with sources
- Memory consolidation (summaries reference originals; nothing is deleted)
- JSON / Markdown export; validated merge / replace import
- Local backups (SQLite + JSON + Markdown), no secrets
- Dashboard from live data; demo data is labelled
- Settings: Ollama URL, models, thresholds, auto-memory, privacy, reset, demo
- start.py / setup.py / main.py launcher (no repeated reinstall)
- Offline fallback when Ollama is down

## Next

- Optional scheduled backups
- Richer conversation search across all threads
- Optional GPU-aware Ollama model recommendations for 8 GB VRAM
- Plugin extractors for notes / files the user explicitly imports
- Multi-user is out of scope (this is a personal, local brain)

## Non-goals

- Cloud sync by default
- Telemetry
- Inventing personal memories
- Replacing the local SQLite graph with a second store
